 | GET | /health | Liveness check. Returns `{"status": "ok"}`. |
 | GET | /users | All users, by id. |
 | GET | /users/<id> | One user, or 404. |
-| POST | /users | Create a user from `{name, email}`. 201, 400 on invalid input, 409 if the email is taken. |
+| POST | /users | Create a user from `{name, email, phone?}`. 201, 400 on invalid input, 409 if the email is taken. |
 
-A user is `{id, name, email}`.
+A user is `{id, name, email, phone}`. `phone` is optional and `null` when not set (including for users created before the field existed).
+
+On create, `phone` (if given and not `null`) must consist of digits, spaces and dashes with an optional leading `+`, and contain 7 to 15 digits in total; otherwise the response is 400 with `"phone is invalid"`.
+
+Existing databases are upgraded by `store.migrate` (migration `002_add_phone.sql` adds a nullable `phone` column); existing rows are kept.
